# BMW 5 Series E12 four-door saloon, 1972-1981.
#
# The first 5-series, and the car that set the BMW three-box pattern for the
# next twenty years: long bonnet, upright four-door cabin, separate boot, twin
# round headlamps each side of a paired kidney grille, chrome bumpers.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_5_Series_(E12)
#
# Dimensions 4.620 x 1.690 x 1.425 m, wheelbase 2.636 m, from the English
# Wikipedia dimension box. Mirrors and rubbing strips take the modelled width
# past the body figure.
#
# Colours. A UK-market colour card for the E12 was not located, so the paint
# names are BMW programme colours of the period, taken from the E21 paint
# register (BMWE21.net, "Paintwork & upholstery colors", which reproduces the
# 1975-79 and 1980-on brochure pages) and applied to the E12 on the evidence
# that BMW used one programme across the range:
#   Polaris metallic  060, offered 1975-1984
#   Schwarz           086, offered 1975-1982
#   Chamonix          085, offered 1975-1979
#   Fjord metallic    037, offered 1975-1979
# Chamonix and Fjord therefore start in June 1975 and retire early; Polaris and
# Schwarz run from launch. This is weaker evidence than a UK colour card and is
# recorded as such rather than presented as confirmed UK availability.
# Weights silver 3, blue 3, black 2, white 2, total 10, provisional pending the
# central rebase.
#
# Speed 185 km/h: between the 520's 160 km/h and the 528i's published 202 km/h,
# the volume UK six-cylinder cars of the late 1970s. Comfort 110/345, on the
# line 180 + 1.5 x 110. Classes 2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence, not production: July 1972 intro, retires staggered
# 1993-1996 on a twenty-one- to twenty-four-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-e12.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-e12.dae (61 objects). References:
# citycars/references/bmw-e12/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted low-poly deviations, recorded rather than corrected: the lower
# bodywork is more angular than the photographs and the bumper curvature is
# simplified. Neither reads at 128 px.

obj=citycar
